    <bpmn:process id="W_W40" name="W40. Regular Price Change Execution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New product setup, category review, or competitive response
Frequency: Ongoing; ~50–100 quantity break rules active at any time
Volume: Primarily bulk-building categories: cement, lumber, nails, screws, paint, plumbing fittings
Owner: Pricing Analyst
Participants: Pricing Analyst, Category Manager
Source: workflow W40 — Regular Price Change Execution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W40_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W40_Lane1" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task21</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W40_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task20</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task24</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task25</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W40_Lane3" name="Pricing Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task22</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task26</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W40_Lane4" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task23</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W40_Lane5" name="Dept. Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W40_End27</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W40_Start7" name="New product setup, category review, or competitive response">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task8" name="Buyer receives vendor price increase notice (letter, email, or portal…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Buyer receives vendor price increase notice (letter, email, or portal notification); enters new cost and effective date in system
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 10 min/vendor notice</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W40_Task9" name="System calculates margin impact: current SRP × current cost vs. current SRP ×…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System calculates margin impact: current SRP × current cost vs. current SRP × new cost; shows margin erosion per SKU and total category impact
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task10" name="Pricing Analyst reviews margin impact report; decides action per SKU: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pricing Analyst reviews margin impact report; decides action per SKU: (a) absorb cost increase (reduce margin), (b) pass through to SRP, (c) increase SRP partially, (d) negotiate with vendor, (e) switch to alternative vendor, (f) discontinue item
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours/vendor notice</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task11" name="Pricing Analyst enters new SRP per SKU with effective date in system; system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Pricing Analyst enters new SRP per SKU with effective date in system; system shows new margin % for validation
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 5 min/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task12" name="Category Manager reviews and approves price changes; VP Merchandising approves…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Category Manager reviews and approves price changes; VP Merchandising approves if aggregate margin impact &gt; PHP 500K/month
Responsible (R): Category Manager / VP
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min – 1 hour/batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W40_Task13" name="System schedules price update: new SRP takes effect at configured date/time…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: System schedules price update: new SRP takes effect at configured date/time (typically start of business day)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow35</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow35</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W40_Task14" name="System pushes updated price file to all POS terminals per nightly sync (or…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: System pushes updated price file to all POS terminals per nightly sync (or immediately if real-time sync configured); updates ecommerce catalog
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow36</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow36</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task15" name="Store Operations receives price change bulletin; Department Supervisors update…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Store Operations receives price change bulletin; Department Supervisors update shelf tags before store opening on effective date
Responsible (R): Dept. Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per price change batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow37</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow37</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W40_Task16" name="System maintains full price history per SKU: date range, old SRP, new SRP…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: System maintains full price history per SKU: date range, old SRP, new SRP, reason code, approver — for audit and BIR compliance
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow38</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow38</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task17" name="Monthly: Pricing Analyst generates price change summary report: # of changes…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Monthly: Pricing Analyst generates price change summary report: # of changes, average increase/decrease, margin impact, top categories affected
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow300</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow300</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task18" name="Buyer receives vendor price protection notice: new lower cost with effective…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Buyer receives vendor price protection notice: new lower cost with effective date (possibly retroactive); enters in system: vendor, SKU(s), old cost, new cost, effective date, scope (future only vs. retroactive)
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow301</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow301</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W40_Task19" name="If retroactive: system calculates credit due based on quantities purchased…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: If retroactive: system calculates credit due based on quantities purchased between effective date and now; generates vendor credit memo per W7.9b
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Cost Accountant
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow302</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow302</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W40_Task20" name="If on-hand inventory exists at old cost: system revalues on-hand inventory to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 13: If on-hand inventory exists at old cost: system revalues on-hand inventory to new cost; posts difference (Dr. Accounts Payable / Cr. COGS or Inventory)
Responsible (R): System / Cost Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Automated + 15 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow303</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow303</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task21" name="Buyer communicates new cost to Pricing Analyst for SRP review per standard W40…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 14: Buyer communicates new cost to Pricing Analyst for SRP review per standard W40 process
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Per W40</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow304</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow304</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task22" name="Pricing Analyst defines quantity break rules per SKU or category in system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 15: Pricing Analyst defines quantity break rules per SKU or category in system: threshold quantity, discount % or fixed price per tier (e.g., cement: 1–9 bags at SRP, 10–99 bags at 5% off, 100+ bags at 8% off); rules are date-effective with start/end dates
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 5 min/rule</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow305</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow305</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task23" name="Category Manager approves quantity break rules; VP Merchandising approves if…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 16: Category Manager approves quantity break rules; VP Merchandising approves if aggregate margin impact exceeds threshold
Responsible (R): Category Manager / VP
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 15 min/batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow306</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow306</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W40_Task24" name="System stores quantity break rules linked to item master; POS automatically…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 17: System stores quantity break rules linked to item master; POS automatically applies the correct tier when scanned quantity meets or exceeds threshold — no cashier intervention required
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow307</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow307</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W40_Task25" name="Discount stacking rules: if a promotional price (W13) is lower than the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 18: Discount stacking rules: if a promotional price (W13) is lower than the quantity break price, system applies the promo price (customer-friendly) and does not stack discounts; if quantity break price is lower, it applies; trade/corporate account pricing (W5B.4c) and quantity break pricing do not stack — the lower of the two applies
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow308</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W40_Flow308</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W40_Task26" name="Monthly: Pricing Analyst reviews quantity break utilization report: frequency…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 19: Monthly: Pricing Analyst reviews quantity break utilization report: frequency of tier triggers by SKU, margin impact, average quantity per transaction for items with quantity breaks, and whether thresholds are driving incremental volume
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow309</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W40_End27" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W40_Flow310</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W40_Annotation28">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-07 (prevent unauthorized pricing changes.) | - operational: Pricing Analyst review and approval gate | ---
Owner: Pricing Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
