    <bpmn:process id="W_W329" name="W329. Competitive Price Tactical Response" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: W130 competitor price intelligence identifies a significant competitive price threat (competitor price on a key SKU ≥ 10% below BuildRight&#x27;s current price, or competitor launches an aggressive promotional campaign on overlapping assortment)
Frequency: ~2–4 tactical responses/month; more frequent during peak competitive periods (year-end sales, &quot;ber&quot; months)
Volume: Each tactical response may affect 10–200 SKUs; typically concentrated in high-visibility categories (cement, paint, tiles, power tools, appliances)
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, Category Manager(s), Pricing Analyst, Supply Planner, VP Store Operations, Marketing Manager
Source: workflow W329 — Competitive Price Tactical Response</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W329_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W329_Lane1" name="Pricing Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W329_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W329_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W329_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W329_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W329_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W329_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W329_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W329_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W329_Lane3" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W329_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W329_Lane4" name="Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W329_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W329_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W329_Start6" name="W130 competitor price intelligence identifies a significant competitive price threat…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W329_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W329_Task7" name="Threat identification and alert">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Threat identification and alert: W130 competitor price intelligence feed flags significant competitive price changes; Pricing Analyst reviews alerts and classifies threat level: (a) Low — isolated SKU, no pattern, no response needed, (b) Medium — multiple SKUs in a category affected, potential customer traffic impact, (c) High — competitor campaign on core categories (cement, paint, lumber), threatensBuildRight&#x27;s price positioning
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W329_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W329_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W329_Task8" name="Impact assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Impact assessment: For Medium and High threats: Category Manager analyzes: (a) sales velocity of affected SKUs (revenue impact if customers switch to competitor), (b) current margin on affected SKUs (room to cut), (c) inventory position (how much stock is at risk of becoming dead if we don&#x27;t respond), (d) historical price elasticity for the category, (e) competitive context — is this a temporary promo or permanent price change?
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W329_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W329_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W329_Task9" name="Response options development">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Response options development: Pricing Analyst and Category Manager prepare response options: (a) Match price — reduce BuildRight price to match competitor (margin sacrifice), (b) Selective match — match on top 10–20 traffic-driving SKUs only, maintain regular price on remainder, (c) Value-add response — keep price but bundle with free delivery, extended warranty, or loyalty bonus points, (d) No response — absorb the competitive threat if margin impact is unacceptable; each option includes projected margin impact, revenue impact, and inventory risk
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W329_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W329_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W329_Task10" name="Decision and approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Decision and approval: VP Merchandising selects response strategy; for margin impact &gt; PHP 500K/month or price reduction &gt; 15% on any SKU: CEO approval required; for margin impact ≤ PHP 500K/month: VP Merchandising approves; decision documented with rationale in system
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CEO (if threshold exceeded)
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W329_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W329_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W329_Task11" name="Price execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Price execution: Pricing Analyst executes approved price changes in pricing master (W289); system propagates: (a) updated prices to POS (within 60 seconds per POS-047), (b) updated prices to ecommerce (within 5 minutes per NFR SLA), (c) updated prices to marketplace channels (W180) if affected SKUs are listed, (d) generates updated shelf labels for stores (W63, W181) — stores receive label reprint instruction with next-day printing deadline
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W329_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W329_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W329_Task12" name="Marketing support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Marketing support: If response includes promotional positioning (&quot;Price Match Guarantee&quot; or &quot;Lowest Price&quot; messaging), Marketing Manager activates pre-approved tactical campaign assets: in-store signage, social media posts, email/SMS to loyalty members; Marketing coordinates with W83 campaign workflow for customer-facing communication
Responsible (R): Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W329_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W329_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W329_Task13" name="Monitoring and exit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monitoring and exit: Pricing Analyst monitors affected SKU sales daily for 14 days post-response: (a) sales volume vs. pre-response baseline, (b) margin impact vs. projection, (c) competitor behavior — have they further reduced prices or returned to normal? At day 14: VP Merchandising decides whether to maintain tactical pricing, transition to permanent price change (W40), or restore original pricing
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 15 min/day for 14 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W329_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W329_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W329_Task14" name="Post-mortem">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-mortem: At day 30, Category Manager prepares tactical response post-mortem: actual vs. projected margin impact, sales volume change, market share assessment (qualitative from W130 data), lessons learned; feeds into quarterly pricing strategy review (W107)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W329_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W329_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W329_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W329_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-241 (ensure controlled execution — Pricing &amp; Promotions (PA-01.2).) | - operational: VP Merchandising review and approval gate
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
