    <bpmn:process id="W_W737" name="W737. Markdown Optimization &amp; Analytics Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly markdown review cycle; or SLOB identification per W220; or end-of-season per W264
Frequency: Weekly (review); continuous (analytics monitoring)
Volume: ~500–1,000 SKUs under markdown consideration at any time; ~2,000–5,000 markdown price changes per month
Owner: Pricing Analyst
Participants: Category Manager, Merchandising Manager, Store Operations (execution per W93)
Source: workflow W737 — Markdown Optimization &amp; Analytics Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W737_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W737_Lane1" name="Pricing Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W737_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W737_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W737_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W737_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W737_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W737_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W737_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W737_Start4" name="Weekly markdown review cycle; or SLOB identification per W220; or end-of-season per W264">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W737_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W737_Task5" name="Weekly markdown candidate identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly markdown candidate identification: Pricing Analyst runs weekly markdown candidate report: (a) criteria for markdown consideration: (i) inventory age &gt;90 days for seasonal items, &gt;180 days for non-seasonal; (ii) sell-through rate &lt;50% of forecast; (iii) weeks of supply &gt;26 weeks (6 months); (iv) SLOB items identified per W220; (v) items approaching end-of-season per W264; (b) for each candidate: current inventory value, weeks of supply, sell-through rate trend, margin at current price, category priority
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1-2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W737_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W737_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W737_Task6" name="Markdown optimization analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Markdown optimization analysis: for each candidate SKU, Pricing Analyst determines optimal markdown: (a) historical markdown response analysis: how did similar items respond to markdowns in past seasons?; (b) price elasticity estimation: at what markdown depth does sell-through accelerate sufficiently?; (c) recovery value optimization: markdown % × projected sell-through = recovery value; find markdown % that maximizes recovery; (d) timing optimization: is it better to mark down now or wait for end-of-season clearance?; (e) cadence: single deep markdown vs. staged markdown (e.g., 20% → 30% → 50% over 6 weeks); (f) present recommendations to Category Manager with supporting data
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2-4 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W737_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W737_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W737_Task7" name="Markdown approval and execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Markdown approval and execution: Category Manager approves markdown strategy: (a) verify markdown does not violate vendor price protection agreements per W161; (b) verify vendor consent if markdown affects vendor-funded inventory; (c) confirm markdown aligns with overall margin plan per W102 category P&amp;L; (d) approved markdowns entered into pricing system per W40 for execution; (e) execution at store level per W93 (markdown &amp; clearance pricing execution); (f) ecommerce price sync per W678 multi-channel pricing consistency
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30-60 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W737_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W737_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W737_Task8" name="Markdown performance tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Markdown performance tracking: weekly, Pricing Analyst tracks markdown performance: (a) for each active markdown: (i) sell-through rate since markdown activation; (ii) remaining inventory and weeks of supply; (iii) actual recovery value vs. projected; (b) identify underperforming markdowns: items not clearing as projected → accelerate to deeper markdown or activate clearance per W532; (c) identify overperforming markdowns: items clearing too fast → potential markdown was too deep, learn for future; (d) final disposition for remaining clearance items: donate per W552, liquidate to jobbers, or dispose per W91
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1-2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W737_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W737_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W737_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W737_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-241 (ensure controlled execution — Pricing &amp; Promotions (PA-01.2).) | - operational: Pricing Analyst review and approval gate
Owner: Pricing Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
