    <bpmn:process id="W_W738" name="W738. Vendor Trade Fund Management &amp; Promotional Budget Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual trade fund negotiation per W155 JBP; or promotional event planning per W83; or monthly trade fund reconciliation
Frequency: Annual (negotiation); per promotional event (commitment); monthly (reconciliation)
Volume: ~20–30 vendor trade fund agreements (top vendors); ~PHP 500M-1B in annual trade fund commitments
Owner: Trade Marketing Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Procurement Manager, Finance Manager, Vendor Account Manager
Source: workflow W738 — Vendor Trade Fund Management &amp; Promotional Budget Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W738_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W738_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W738_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W738_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W738_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W738_Lane2" name="Trade Marketing Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W738_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W738_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W738_Lane3" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W738_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W738_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W738_Start5" name="Annual trade fund negotiation per W155 JBP; or promotional event planning per W83; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W738_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W738_Task6" name="Annual trade fund negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual trade fund negotiation: during annual joint business planning per W155: (a) Category Manager and Trade Marketing Manager negotiate trade fund commitments with each top-20 vendor: (i) annual trade fund amount (typically 2-5% of projected annual purchases); (ii) fund allocation by activity: in-store promotions, co-op advertising, display fees, new product launch support, seasonal campaigns; (iii) fund accrual method: lump sum, quarterly accrual based on purchases, or per-event; (iv) fund utilization criteria: what activities qualify, documentation requirements, proof-of-performance; (v) fund expiration: unused funds at year-end — carried forward or forfeited; (b) document agreed terms in trade fund agreement per W402 contract master; (c) Finance reviews fund terms for margin impact per W85
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Trade Marketing Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2-4 hours per vendor negotiation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W738_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W738_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W738_Task7" name="Promotional event fund commitment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Promotional event fund commitment: when promotional event is planned per W83: (a) Trade Marketing Manager identifies which vendors should contribute based on: (i) products featured in the promotion; (ii) vendor trade fund balance available; (iii) historical vendor contribution for similar events; (b) calculate vendor contribution: (i) co-op advertising share: % of media spend allocated to vendor&#x27;s products; (ii) in-store display cost: fixture, signage, and space allocation; (iii) promotional markdown funding: vendor&#x27;s share of promotional price reduction; (c) obtain vendor agreement on contribution amount per W513 vendor-funded promotional activity; (d) book commitment against vendor&#x27;s trade fund balance in system
Responsible (R): Trade Marketing Mgr
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1-2 hours per promotional event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W738_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W738_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W738_Task8" name="Monthly trade fund reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly trade fund reconciliation: Finance Manager and Trade Marketing Manager reconcile monthly: (a) for each vendor with active trade fund: (i) opening fund balance; (ii) additions: new accruals from purchases during the month; (iii) deductions: commitments for promotional activities, co-op advertising, display costs, markdown funding; (iv) proof-of-performance documentation: did the promotional activity actually occur? Were the agreed terms met?; (v) closing fund balance; (b) resolve discrepancies: (i) vendor disputes BuildRight&#x27;s deduction: provide proof-of-performance documentation; (ii) BuildRight identifies underfunded activity: negotiate additional vendor contribution; (iii) unused fund balance approaching expiration: propose utilization plan; (c) reconciliation shared with vendor for agreement
Responsible (R): Trade Marketing Mgr / Finance Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2-4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W738_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W738_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W738_Task9" name="Quarterly trade fund effectiveness review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly trade fund effectiveness review: Category Manager reviews trade fund ROI quarterly: (a) for each vendor&#x27;s trade fund: (i) total vendor funding received; (ii) incremental sales generated by vendor-funded promotions; (iii) incremental margin after deducting BuildRight&#x27;s execution cost; (iv) ROI = incremental margin / vendor funding; (b) benchmark vendors: which vendors provide the highest trade fund ROI?; (c) identify underperforming trade fund allocations: redirect to higher-ROI activities in next negotiation; (d) insights feed into next annual negotiation per W155 JBP
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Trade Marketing Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4-6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W738_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W738_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W738_Task10" name="Year-end trade fund settlement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Year-end trade fund settlement: at fiscal year-end: (a) Finance Manager conducts final reconciliation for all vendor trade funds: (i) total accrued vs. total utilized vs. total remaining; (b) for unused funds: (i) if agreement allows carry-forward: roll balance to next year; (ii) if funds expire: negotiate with vendor for extension or reallocation; (iii) if funds are non-refundable credits: apply against AP balance per W7; (c) prepare year-end trade fund summary for each vendor; (d) archive all documentation per W256 retention policy
Responsible (R): Finance Manager / Trade Marketing Mgr
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2-3 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W738_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W738_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W738_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
