    <bpmn:process id="W_W1231" name="W1231. Store-Level Construction Material Price Volatility Monitoring &amp; Dynamic Cost Adjustment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly vendor price bulletin or commodity market index update for key construction materials (cement, steel rebar, lumber, copper wire, PVC pipe)
Frequency: Weekly monitoring; dynamic adjustments as triggered
Volume: ~200 stores × ~50 volatile SKUs monitored = 10,000 SKU-store price observations/week
Owner: Pricing Analyst
Participants: Pricing Analyst, Category Manager, Store Manager, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1231 — Store-Level Construction Material Price Volatility Monitoring &amp; Dynamic Cost Adjustment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1231_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1231_Lane1" name="Pricing Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1231_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1231_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1231_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1231_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1231_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1231_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1231_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1231_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1231_Lane3" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1231_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1231_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1231_Start5" name="Weekly vendor price bulletin or commodity market index update for key construction…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1231_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1231_Task6" name="Weekly commodity price intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly commodity price intake: Pricing Analyst receives vendor price bulletins, monitors DTI Suggested Retail Price advisories for cement, and tracks commodity indices (steel, copper)
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1231_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1231_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1231_Task7" name="Cost impact analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cost impact analysis: Calculate cost change impact per SKU: (a) new landed cost vs. current WAC; (b) margin impact at current SRP; (c) competitive price position vs. last known competitor prices per W130
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1231_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1231_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1231_Task8" name="Price adjustment recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Price adjustment recommendation: Generate price adjustment proposal: (a) SKUs requiring SRP increase (cost up, margin below floor); (b) SKUs requiring SRP decrease (cost down, price uncompetitive); (c) hold recommendations (within tolerance band); (d) impact on loyalty pricing, trade pricing, and corporate contract pricing per W40
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1231_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1231_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1231_Task9" name="Category Manager review and approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Category Manager review and approval: Category Manager reviews proposals: (a) approve standard adjustments (within ±5% of current SRP); (b) escalate adjustments &gt;5% to VP Merchandising; (c) consider competitive positioning, inventory position, and seasonal demand per W130 and W31
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1231_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1231_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1231_Task10" name="System price update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: System price update: Approved price changes loaded into ERP: (a) update SRP in item master; (b) auto-propagate to POS (near-real-time per event streaming), ecommerce (per continuous push), and loyalty/trade pricing matrices; (c) generate shelf label update file per W63 for affected stores; (d) set effective date/time for price change
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1231_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1231_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1231_Task11" name="Store execution monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Store execution monitoring: (a) push price change notification to Store Managers via mobile app; (b) Store Manager or Stock Associate updates shelf labels within 24 hours per W63; (c) POS auto-applies new pricing regardless of shelf label timing — system price is truth
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1231_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1231_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1231_Task12" name="Post-adjustment analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-adjustment analytics: After 1 week: (a) analyze sales volume impact of price change; (b) compare actual margin vs. projected; (c) flag any stores with shelf label compliance gaps; (d) feed data back into W31 demand forecasting
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1231_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1231_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1231_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1231_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-241 (ensure controlled execution — Pricing &amp; Promotions (PA-01.2).) | - operational: Pricing Analyst review and approval gate
Owner: Pricing Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
